    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nHi,\r\n\r\nI encountered an issue when opening mini.files on a new or unsaved file. \r\n\r\nmini.files fails to open and throws the error mentioned below.\r\n\r\nI suggest adding a dialog prompt that appears when the file is new or unsaved, with options like:\r\n\r\nPrompt message: \"Would you like to save the file before opening mini.\r\n\t\tIf \"Yes,\" the file is saved, and then mini.files opens as expected.\r\n\t\tIf \"No,\" mini.files opens without including the unsaved file.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, I'd be happy to attempt implementing this feature if you're open to it.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nv0.10.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim test.ts`\r\n2. open mini.files\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nmini.files opening\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe plugin fails to open and shows the following error:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d483da8c-4aa0-49c7-b9c9-7c76f4ca8a99)",
